Recovery zone distribution


Show code
cycles |&gt;
  filter(!is.na(rec_zone)) |&gt;
  count(month, rec_zone) |&gt;
  group_by(month) |&gt;
  mutate(pct = n / sum(n)) |&gt;
  ungroup() |&gt;
  ggplot(aes(x = month, y = pct, fill = rec_zone)) +
  geom_col(width = 25) +
  scale_fill_manual(
    values = c(Green = "#1D9E75", Yellow = "#BA7517", Red = "#E24B4A"),
    name = "Zone"
  ) +
  scale_x_date(date_breaks = "2 months", date_labels = "%b '%y") +
  scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::percent) +
  labs(
    title    = "Monthly recovery zone composition",
    subtitle = "Stack shows proportion of Green / Yellow / Red days per month",
    x = NULL, y = "Proportion of days"
  ) +
  theme_whoop()





Monthly proportion of days in each recovery zone, showing how readiness varied across the year.

Deep sleep and REM over time
Deep sleep (slow-wave sleep) is critical for physical recovery; REM is linked to cognitive consolidation. Here we track their 4-week rolling means separately.


Show code
main_sleeps |&gt;
  filter(!is.na(deep_min), !is.na(rem_min)) |&gt;
  arrange(date) |&gt;
  mutate(
    deep_roll = rollmean(deep_min, 28, fill = NA, align = "right", na.rm = TRUE),
    rem_roll  = rollmean(rem_min,  28, fill = NA, align = "right", na.rm = TRUE)
  ) |&gt;
  pivot_longer(cols = c(deep_roll, rem_roll), names_to = "metric", values_to = "minutes") |&gt;
  mutate(metric = recode(metric, deep_roll = "Deep (SWS)", rem_roll = "REM")) |&gt;
  ggplot(aes(x = date, y = minutes, color = metric)) +
  geom_line(linewidth = 1.1, na.rm = TRUE) +
  scale_color_manual(values = c("Deep (SWS)" = "#3266ad", "REM" = "#1D9E75"), name = NULL) +
  scale_x_date(date_breaks = "2 months", date_labels = "%b '%y") +
  labs(
    title    = "Deep sleep and REM — 28-day rolling mean",
    subtitle = "Smoothed trajectories showing longer-term trends",
    x = NULL, y = "Minutes per night"
  ) +
  theme_whoop()





4-week rolling mean of nightly deep and REM sleep (minutes). Both series are smoothed to reduce nightly noise. Deep sleep shows a gradual upward trend through mid-2023; REM peaks in January 2024.
